Control [SimTalk] - Checkbox
Sets the control which the Checkbox designated by <Path> executes.
Remarks
Plant Simulation calls the Control when the value changes when you click the object.
Plant Simulation only calls the Control of the object itself, not of instances of the object.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Control:method
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Example
MyCheckbox.Control := "myControl"
See also
Control [Checkbox]
Control [SimTalk] - Checkbox
Plant Simulation Help 11-5179
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Value [SimTalk] - Checkbox
Activates (true) or deactivates (false) the Checkbox designated by <Path>. The Checkbox executes a
Control when its value changes.
Syntax
<Path>.Value:boolean
Watchable
The attribute is watchable.
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
MyCheckbox.Value := false
See also
Value [drop-down list] - Checkbox
Control [Checkbox]
Button
Button [object]
Use the object Button for showing a button in the Frame. When you click the button, it executes the action
which you programmed in a control.
Image
Description
The Button executes the action, which you programmed in the Control, when the user clicks it.
If you type in a label for the button, Plant Simulation shows that label on the button in the Frame.
